A sum of ₹10,000 is invested at a compound interest rate of 10% per annum for 2 years. What is the compound interest earned?

A) ₹2,000
B) ₹2,100
C) ₹2,200
D) ₹2,500

Answer: B) ₹2,100

Explanation:

Amount after 2 years:

A=P\left(1+\frac{R}{100}\right)^T $$ $$ A=10000(1.1)^2 $$ $$ A=10000\times1.21=₹12,100 $$

Compound Interest:

CI=A-P 
=12100−10000=
₹2,100
